{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3446","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3446","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3446\",\"parent_revision\":\"74d3616f27ce5a337b939dd535dad78ba13f5c39b20815fd07f21c0730dc1a1f\",\"root_revision\":\"74d3616f27ce5a337b939dd535dad78ba13f5c39b20815fd07f21c0730dc1a1f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\ndevelopment-harness ships .codex-plugin and .cursor-plugin manifests, so it claims support for harnesses beyond Claude Code. Its task-state tracking runs on one, because neither manifest declares hooks. Both harnesses support plugin-bundled hooks, so this is a packaging and adapter gap rather than a harness limitation.\\n\\nRefiled from #3437, which accumulated four correction comments, three of which corrected the one before. Its body was wrong in three places and its conclusion was replaced. Everything below is the corrected state; the superseded item is retained for the provenance trail.\\n\\nWHAT EACH HARNESS SUPPLIES AT SUBAGENT STOP\\n\\nVerified against vendor documentation and, where noted, harness source. All accessed 2026-09-06 \u2014 this table is a claim about that date and should be re-read before it is relied on.\\n\\n| Harness | Stop event | Session id scope | Per-subagent id at stop | Final message in payload |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Claude Code | SubagentStop | parent | agent_id | last_assistant_message |\\n| Codex | SubagentStop | parent, stated in docs | agent_id | last_assistant_message |\\n| Cursor | subagentStop | parent (conversation_id) | absent \u2014 subagent_id is on subagentStart only | summary, plus task and description |\\n| Hermes | subagent_stop | parent_session_id | child_session_id, nullable; the stable child_subagent_id is start-side only | child_summary |\\n| Kimi Code | SubagentStop | session_id, scope undocumented | not documented | not documented |\\n| OpenCode | none | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 |\\n\\nOpenCode has no subagent event. Its documented event list contains none, and the SubagentStop reported earlier came from a third-party npm shim that synthesises it by intercepting tool.execute.after on the Task tool. Its closest analogue is session.idle.\\n\\nWHAT THIS MAKES POSSIBLE\\n\\nFour of the five harnesses with the event supply the sub-agent's final message directly in the payload. That is the field carrying the STATUS line, so the transcript-scanning parser in task_status_hook.py is a fallback rather than the mechanism, and a payload adapter reading one field covers Claude Code, Codex, Cursor and Hermes.\\n\\nCursor additionally supplies task and description, so the task is recoverable there without any identifier.\\n\\nCodex uses the same hooks/hooks.json plugin layout as Claude Code, and exports CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT to hook processes as a documented compatibility shim, so the existing hook file is already in the location Codex looks for.\\n\\nWHAT IS NOT DECISIVE\\n\\nWhether a harness exposes a per-subagent identity at stop. That figure was stated three times in the superseded item, each time as load-bearing, and it decides nothing: under a key derived from plan address and task id, identity is needed only for one fallback tier. Recorded above as reference detail so it is not re-litigated.\\n\\nDEPENDS ON\\n\\nThe correlation-key defect must be settled first. A hook that fires but cannot say which task stopped is worse than no hook.\\n\\nACCEPTANCE\\n\\nEither the .codex-plugin and .cursor-plugin manifests declare hooks and the handler reads the payload's final-message field per harness, or each manifest carries a one-line note that hook-based task-state tracking is Claude Code only. Not a third option.\\n\\nUser-provided context: Kimi, OpenCode and Hermes have not been checked for whether a plugin can bundle hooks as distinct from a user configuring them. Kimi's hook rules are documented as user configuration in config.toml.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Refiled from #3437 after four rounds of correction, 2026-09-06\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"55a44c54bd6e5a8def18d51a908431cb1bf9288b97408195d5f55b90f30a82e7\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABTSBNgA\"}"}